# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Build output. The icons under build/ are generated by tools/genicons.py and
# committed, so a clone needs neither Python nor Pillow to build; the binaries
# beside them are not.
build/bin/
frontend/dist/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/package.json.md5
installer/build/bin/
installer/frontend/wailsjs/
dist-installer/
build/darwin/
SymChit.dmg
# builddmg.sh stages the bundle here before create-dmg runs and removes it
# afterwards. It is listed because a build that stops in the middle leaves it
# behind; a staged copy of the whole application is not a thing to commit.
dist-dmg/

# What build_flatpak.sh leaves behind. The list is cleanup_flatpak.sh's, which
# is the one place that knows what the build writes: the bundle, the two
# working directories, flatpak-builder's own cache, the manifest and the
# desktop and metainfo files. All six are generated from VERSION and the
# product's own names at build time, so a committed copy would be a second
# statement of things that already have one home.
symchit.flatpak
.flatpak-build/
.flatpak-repo/
.flatpak-builder/
uk.codecrafter.SymChit.yml
packaging/

# What an operating system leaves in a folder it has been shown. Neither is
# ours and neither means anything to anybody else; the macOS one arrives on
# every folder the DMG build touches.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# installer/payload.zip is deliberately NOT ignored: it is committed as an
# empty-zip placeholder so `go build ./...` works in a fresh clone. build.ps1
# stages the real payload into it and puts the placeholder back afterwards, so
# a payload of megabytes never reaches a commit.

# Wails writes its generated bindings here. They are not the wire contract:
# frontend/src/api.ts is, and tests/structural/wire_test.go compares it with
# the Go DTOs.
frontend/wailsjs/

# Local scratch notes.
NOTES.md
resume.md
.claude/resume.md
